<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://huy-quang-dao.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://huy-quang-dao.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-11-26T00:36:02+00:00</updated><id>https://huy-quang-dao.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>Quang Huy Dao is a robotics engineer at VinMotion working on humanoid motion, fall recovery, and learning-based control. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">InstantTrack, one month in: 35 repos and 4 papers</title><link href="https://huy-quang-dao.github.io/blog/2026/instanttrack-one-month-in/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="InstantTrack, one month in: 35 repos and 4 papers"/><published>2026-11-26T03:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-11-26T03:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://huy-quang-dao.github.io/blog/2026/instanttrack-one-month-in</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://huy-quang-dao.github.io/blog/2026/instanttrack-one-month-in/"><![CDATA[<p>On 29 October I released <a href="https://github.com/Huy-Quang-Dao/instantTrack">InstantTrack</a>: one whole-body motion-tracking policy for all 40 LAFAN1 clips (2.45 h of motion) on the Unitree G1, trained on one RTX 5090 in 15 minutes. Four weeks later it trains in under 3 minutes, and other people have built on it in ways I did not plan for. This post records both.</p> <figure> <video src="/assets/video/instanttrack.mp4" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="auto" height="auto" autoplay="" loop="" muted=""/> <figcaption class="caption">Same 6 minutes of training on fallAndGetUp2_subject3: SuperMimic + EMA, InstantTrack v1.1, and InstantTrack v1.2. Faint blue ghost: reference motion.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="from-15-minutes-to-under-3">From 15 minutes to under 3</h2> <p>Every release is measured the same way: train until the deployed policy reaches a normalized return of 0.82 with 0 of 40 clips failed, and holds it for three checkpoints in a row. The baseline is SuperMimic with a policy EMA on the same machine, simulator, MDP and evaluator, which takes 0.55 h.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th style="text-align: left">Release</th> <th style="text-align: left">Date</th> <th style="text-align: right">Time to target</th> <th style="text-align: right">vs SuperMimic + EMA</th> <th style="text-align: left">What changed</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">v1.0</td> <td style="text-align: left">29 Oct</td> <td style="text-align: right">15 min</td> <td style="text-align: right">2.2×</td> <td style="text-align: left">SuperMimic-style world model with an InstantMimic-style GPU training loop</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">v1.1</td> <td style="text-align: left">30 Oct</td> <td style="text-align: right">11.4 min</td> <td style="text-align: right">2.8×</td> <td style="text-align: left">The policy outputs a correction to the reference pose</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">v1.2</td> <td style="text-align: left">1 Nov</td> <td style="text-align: right">7.2 min</td> <td style="text-align: right">4.7×</td> <td style="text-align: left">Muon for the hidden weight matrices, CUDA-graph captured updates, one goal-encoder pass per rollout</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">v1.3</td> <td style="text-align: left">4 Nov</td> <td style="text-align: right">≤ 3 min</td> <td style="text-align: right">≥ 10.9×</td> <td style="text-align: left">BlinkMimic’s changes merged back: structured world model, mirror augmentation, evaluation-guided resets, overlapped CUDA streams</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">v1.4</td> <td style="text-align: left">7 Nov</td> <td style="text-align: right">2.74 min</td> <td style="text-align: right"> </td> <td style="text-align: left">Overlapped critic update, 11.87 it/s (from 10.28)</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">v1.4.1</td> <td style="text-align: left">23 Nov</td> <td style="text-align: right"> </td> <td style="text-align: right"> </td> <td style="text-align: left"><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">CITATION.cff</code> and a Zenodo DOI</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>From v1.3 on, checkpoints are evaluated every 100 iterations instead of every 1.5 to 3 minutes, so the times are finer than the old schedule could show. The v1.4 figure is the mean of 15 seeds (range 2.21–3.61 min). The <a href="https://github.com/Huy-Quang-Dao/instantTrack/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">changelog</a> has every run, including the changes that did not help.</p> <h2 id="a-fork-that-came-back">A fork that came back</h2> <p>The biggest single step, v1.2 to v1.3, did not come from me. Fuyi Chen forked InstantTrack v1.2, made it faster and released it as <a href="https://github.com/fuyichen0725/blinkmimic">BlinkMimic</a>. Because both projects are MIT-licensed, I could merge those changes back into InstantTrack v1.3 with credit, and then build v1.4 on top. BlinkMimic was in turn rebuilt in JAX as <a href="https://github.com/nico-bohlinger/xmimic">XMimic</a>, which trains the same task in under a minute on four H100s.</p> <p>That loop is the main reason I keep the code open and every run logged: someone else can pick up a result, check it, and push it further than I would alone.</p> <h2 id="who-builds-on-instanttrack">Who builds on InstantTrack</h2> <p>Below are the papers that cite InstantTrack and the public repositories I found that build on its code, carry its training recipe to new robots, run it as a backend or baseline, or teach it.</p> <style>.itu-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(96px,1fr));gap:.6rem;margin:1rem 0 1.5rem}.itu-stat{border:1px solid var(--global-divider-color);border-radius:.6rem;padding:.8rem .6rem;text-align:center;background:var(--global-card-bg-color)}.itu-stat b{display:block;font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1.1;color:var(--global-theme-color);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.itu-stat b *{color:inherit}.itu-stat>span{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light)}.itu-tree{display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:0;overflow-x:auto;padding:.25rem 0 .75rem;margin-bottom:.5rem}.itu-gen{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:.35rem;min-width:128px;position:relative;padding:0 .9rem}.itu-gen+.itu-gen::before{content:"\f054";font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-weight:900;position:absolute;left:-0.35rem;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--global-text-color-light);font-size:.75rem}.itu-gen h6{font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--global-text-color-light);margin:0 0 .2rem;text-align:center}.itu-node{display:block;font-size:.8rem;padding:.2rem .55rem;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--global-divider-color);text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;color:var(--global-text-color)!important;background:var(--global-card-bg-color)}a.itu-node:hover{border-color:var(--global-theme-color);text-decoration:none}.itu-node.itu-me{background:var(--global-theme-color);border-color:var(--global-theme-color);color:#fff!important;font-weight:600;font-size:.95rem;padding:.45rem .8rem}.itu-node.itu-root{border-style:dashed;color:var(--global-text-color-light)!important}.itu-group{margin-top:1.6rem}.itu-group h3{font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:.15rem}.itu-group h3 i{color:var(--global-theme-color);margin-right:.35rem}.itu-group h3 small{color:var(--global-text-color-light);font-size:.8rem;margin-left:.3rem}.itu-group>p{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light);margin-bottom:.6rem}.itu-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:.6rem}.itu-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--global-divider-color);border-radius:.6rem;padding:.6rem .75rem;background:var(--global-card-bg-color);color:var(--global-text-color)!important;transition:transform .15s,border-color .15s}.itu-card:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);border-color:var(--global-theme-color);text-decoration:none}.itu-card-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:.5rem}.itu-card-top strong{font-size:.95rem}.itu-card-top .itu-star{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light);white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.itu-card-top .itu-star i{color:#e3b341}.itu-owner{font-size:.72rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light)}.itu-note{font-size:.8rem;margin-top:.3rem;line-height:1.35}.itu-bar{height:3px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--global-divider-color);margin-top:auto;padding-top:0}.itu-bar>i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:2px;background:var(--global-theme-color);opacity:.8}.itu-chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.35rem}.itu-chips a{font-size:.75rem;padding:.15rem .55rem;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--global-divider-color);color:var(--global-text-color-light)!important}.itu-chips a:hover{border-color:var(--global-theme-color);text-decoration:none}.itu-foot{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light);margin-top:1rem}.itu-papers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(100%,340px),1fr));gap:.6rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem}.itu-paper{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem;border:1px solid var(--global-divider-color);border-left:3px solid var(--global-theme-color);border-radius:.4rem;padding:.65rem .8rem;background:var(--global-card-bg-color);color:var(--global-text-color)!important;transition:border-color .15s}.itu-paper:hover{border-color:var(--global-theme-color);text-decoration:none}.itu-paper .itu-venue{font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--global-theme-color);font-weight:600}.itu-paper strong{font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.3}.itu-paper .itu-authors{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light)}.itu-paper blockquote{margin:.2rem 0 0;padding:0 0 0 .6rem;border-left:2px solid var(--global-divider-color);font-size:.8rem;font-style:italic;line-height:1.4;color:var(--global-text-color)}.itu-paper .itu-result{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--global-text-color-light)}.itu-paper .itu-result i{color:var(--global-theme-color);margin-right:.25rem}</style> <div class="itu-stats"> <div class="itu-stat"><b>35</b><span>public repos build on, port or cite it</span></div> <div class="itu-stat"><b>9.1k</b><span>combined stars of those repos</span></div> <div class="itu-stat"><b><span data-github-stars="Huy-Quang-Dao/instantTrack"><span class="stars-count">218</span></span></b><span>stars on InstantTrack</span></div> <div class="itu-stat"><b>4</b><span>papers and write-ups cite it</span></div> <div class="itu-stat"><b>15</b><span>direct forks</span></div> <div class="itu-stat"><b>4</b><span>generations of follow-up work</span></div> </div> <div class="itu-group" id="itu-papers" style="margin-top:0"> <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-scroll"></i>Cited in papers<small>4</small></h3> <p>Research papers and technical write-ups that cite InstantTrack, with the sentence that cites it.</p> <div class="itu-papers"> <a class="itu-paper" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.16422"> <span class="itu-venue">arXiv 2611.16422</span> <strong>BlinkMimic: Training a Humanoid Motion Tracker in Minutes on a Single GPU</strong> <span class="itu-authors">Fuyi Chen</span> <blockquote>“InstantTrack (Dao, 2026) introduced EMA deployment, Muon and a reference residual in an open implementation. We build on this line.”</blockquote> </a> <a class="itu-paper" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.20452"> <span class="itu-venue">arXiv 2611.20452</span> <strong>XMimic and XSoma: Learning Humanoid Motion Tracking and Locomotion in Under a Minute</strong> <span class="itu-authors">Nico Bohlinger, Jan Peters</span> <blockquote>“InstantTrack and BlinkMimic then reduced the time to learn all 40 clips of the LAFAN1 dataset on the Unitree G1 to about 3 minutes on a single consumer GPU.”</blockquote> </a> <a class="itu-paper" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.27648"> <span class="itu-venue">arXiv 2611.27648</span> <strong>Trust What Repeats: Capped World-Model Policy Gradients for Humanoid Motion Tracking</strong> <span class="itu-authors">Xuzhe Dang, Stefan Edelkamp</span> <blockquote>“InstantTrack and BlinkMimic speed up SuperMimic's line with a different optimizer, a residual policy, GPU graph capture [...] and train 40 LAFAN1 clips in minutes.”</blockquote> </a> <a class="itu-paper" href="https://www.dollhouserobots.com/posts/super-gpc"> <span class="itu-venue">Blog post, 25 Nov 2026</span> <strong>SuperGPC: training a humanoid autoregressive motion policy fast, on one GPU</strong> <span class="itu-authors">Carlos Diaz-Padron (Dollhouse)</span> <blockquote>“We integrated this work, and a mix of the optimizations from follow up projects InstantTrack (Dao, 2026), and BlinkMimic (Chen, 2026).”</blockquote> <span class="itu-result"><i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i>Generative Pretrained Controllers pipeline: about 8.5 days to about 30 hours of training on one RTX 5090</span> </a> </div> </div> <div class="itu-tree" aria-label="Lineage of projects around InstantTrack"> <div class="itu-gen"> <h6>Roots</h6> <span class="itu-node itu-root">SuperMimic</span> <a class="itu-node itu-root" href="https://github.com/zita-ch/supermimic_vibed">supermimic_vibed</a> <span class="itu-node itu-root">InstantMimic</span> </div> <div class="itu-gen"> <h6>Gen 0</h6> <span class="itu-node itu-me">InstantTrack</span> </div> <div class="itu-gen"> <h6>Gen 1</h6> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/fuyichen0725/blinkmimic">BlinkMimic</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/kaibohex/muscle-supermimic">muscle-supermimic</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/Motphys/Uni-SuperMimic">Uni-SuperMimic</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/IoET-y/robot-skill-factory">robot-skill-factory</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/RoboticsResearchHubVN/InstantAMP">InstantAMP</a> </div> <div class="itu-gen"> <h6>Gen 2</h6> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/nico-bohlinger/xmimic">XMimic</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/Roboparty/PartyMimic">PartyMimic</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/wbc-mjlab/wbc-mjlab">wbc-mjlab</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/Frank-ZY-Dou/ndm-gym">NDM Gym</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/jyl681/blinkmimic2">BlinkMimic 2</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/VittorioPastore/m1mic-mlx">M1mic-MLX</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/cyclo_mjlab">cyclo_mjlab</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://www.dollhouserobots.com/posts/super-gpc">SuperGPC</a> </div> <div class="itu-gen"> <h6>Gen 3</h6> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/nico-bohlinger/xsoma">XSoma</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/fei-yang-wu/RLOpt">RLOpt</a> <a class="itu-node" href="https://github.com/MyoHub/myosuite">MyoSuite</a> </div> </div> <div class="itu-group" id="itu-derived"> <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-code-branch"></i>Built on InstantTrack's code<small>13 repos</small></h3> <p>Their license notices name InstantTrack as code they derive from, directly or through BlinkMimic.</p> <div class="itu-cards"> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/fuyichen0725/blinkmimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>BlinkMimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 331</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> fuyichen0725</span> <span class="itu-note">G1 tracking in ~3 min; derives directly from InstantTrack</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="726"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/nico-bohlinger/xmimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>XMimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 206</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> nico-bohlinger</span> <span class="itu-note">BlinkMimic's trainer rebuilt in JAX; benchmarks InstantTrack v1.3</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="453"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/Roboparty/PartyMimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>PartyMimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 199</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> Roboparty</span> <span class="itu-note">Quick, precise, versatile humanoid mimic</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="437"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/wbc-mjlab/wbc-mjlab"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>wbc-mjlab</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 186</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> wbc-mjlab</span> <span class="itu-note">Universal whole-body tracking in mjlab</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="409"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/Frank-ZY-Dou/ndm-gym"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>NDM Gym</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 93</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> Frank-ZY-Dou</span> <span class="itu-note">Neural world models; ships a BlinkMimic/InstantTrack algorithm</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="206"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/jyl681/blinkmimic2"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>BlinkMimic 2</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 69</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> jyl681</span> <span class="itu-note">One policy for all 129,491 BONES-SEED clips</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="153"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/nico-bohlinger/xsoma"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>XSoma</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 34</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> nico-bohlinger</span> <span class="itu-note">Rough-terrain velocity tracking in under a minute</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="77"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/RoboticsResearchHubVN/InstantAMP"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>InstantAMP</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 32</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> RoboticsResearchHubVN</span> <span class="itu-note">AMP in 30 min on one RTX 5090</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="72"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/shangchaohu718/PERA"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>PERA</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 28</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> shangchaohu718</span> <span class="itu-note">Plug-in experts for continual whole-body control</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="63"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/VittorioPastore/m1mic-mlx"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>M1mic-MLX</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 27</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> VittorioPastore</span> <span class="itu-note">Train the G1 tracker on a MacBook with MLX</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="61"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/cyclo_mjlab"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>cyclo_mjlab</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 6</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> ROBOTIS-GIT</span> <span class="itu-note">ROBOTIS's mjlab toolkit for their robots</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="15"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/fei-yang-wu/RLOpt"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>RLOpt</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 5</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> fei-yang-wu</span> <span class="itu-note">RL with advanced optimization techniques</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="13"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/TonyInvent/MacMimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>MacMimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 1</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> TonyInvent</span> <span class="itu-note">OpenSprite humanoid trained on a MacBook Pro</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="4"></i></div> </a> </div> </div> <div class="itu-group" id="itu-recipe"> <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-flask"></i>Port the training recipe<small>4 repos</small></h3> <p>They carry InstantTrack's ideas (Muon split, policy EMA, no-sync loop, structured world model) to new bodies and simulators.</p> <div class="itu-cards"> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/MyoHub/myosuite"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>MyoSuite</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 1291</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> MyoHub</span> <span class="itu-note">Musculoskeletal tracking; ships the BlinkMimic-InstantTrack license</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="2825"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/Motphys/Uni-SuperMimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>Uni-SuperMimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 319</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> Motphys</span> <span class="itu-note">SuperMimic on UniLab; follows InstantTrack's Muon split</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="700"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/kaibohex/muscle-supermimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>muscle-supermimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 55</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> kaibohex</span> <span class="itu-note">3.9 h to 1.8 h on MS-Human-700 with the InstantTrack recipe</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="122"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/kkmjj0721/quadruped_supermimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>quadruped_supermimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 31</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> kkmjj0721</span> <span class="itu-note">World-model tracking for the Go2 quadruped</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="70"></i></div> </a> </div> </div> <div class="itu-group" id="itu-run"> <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-gauge-high"></i>Run, benchmark or reproduce it<small>4 repos</small></h3> <p>InstantTrack as a backend, a baseline or a policy on a real robot stack.</p> <div class="itu-cards"> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/IoET-y/robot-skill-factory"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>robot-skill-factory</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 61</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> IoET-y</span> <span class="itu-note">Uses InstantTrack as its training backend, with patches</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="136"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/basicv8vc/modded-supermimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>modded-supermimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 2</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> basicv8vc</span> <span class="itu-note">G1 speedrun benchmark; InstantTrack v1.4 baseline</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="7"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/zzw705140-cpu/instanttrack-Repro"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>InstantTrack-Repro</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 0</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> zzw705140-cpu</span> <span class="itu-note">End-to-end reproduction of InstantTrack</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="2"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/ETHRoboticsClub/v1-walk-demo"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>ETHRC V1 walk demo</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 0</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> ETHRoboticsClub</span> <span class="itu-note">ETH Robotics Club humanoid runs an InstantTrack policy in the browser</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="2"></i></div> </a> </div> </div> <div class="itu-group" id="itu-lists"> <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-book-open"></i>Featured in lists, courses and notes<small>5 repos</small></h3> <p>Curated indexes and tutorials that teach or track InstantTrack.</p> <div class="itu-cards"> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/datawhalechina/every-embodied"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>every-embodied</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 4574</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> datawhalechina</span> <span class="itu-note">Datawhale course: a chapter on InstantTrack and BlinkMimic speed-ups</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="10002"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/ImChong/Robotics_Notebooks"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>Robotics Notebooks</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 870</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> ImChong</span> <span class="itu-note">Robotics wiki with an InstantTrack entity page</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="1904"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/miao-org/awesome-supermimic"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>awesome-supermimic</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 655</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> miao-org</span> <span class="itu-note">Curated SuperMimic implementations</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="1434"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/bjrobotnewbie/RobotNewbieDocs"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>RobotNewbieDocs</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 8</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> bjrobotnewbie</span> <span class="itu-note">Beginner robotics docs</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="20"></i></div> </a> <a class="itu-card" href="https://github.com/QinnyuLan/SuperMimicCarnival"> <div class="itu-card-top"> <strong>SuperMimicCarnival</strong> <span class="itu-star"><i class="fa-solid fa-star"></i> 3</span> </div> <span class="itu-owner"><i class="fa-brands fa-github"></i> QinnyuLan</span> <span class="itu-note">Index of verified SuperMimic reproductions</span> <div class="itu-bar" style="margin-top:0.5rem"><i data-w="9"></i></div> </a> </div> </div> <div class="itu-group"> <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-ellipsis"></i>And more<small>9 repos</small></h3> <p>Forks of forks, lab notes and blog posts that also credit InstantTrack.</p> <div class="itu-chips"> <a href="https://github.com/UNITYIIPP/partymimic">UNITYIIPP/partymimic</a><a href="https://github.com/Khanhtkp/xsoma_run">Khanhtkp/xsoma_run</a><a href="https://github.com/EchoXuK/Supermimc-CarryBox">EchoXuK/Supermimc-CarryBox</a><a href="https://github.com/Hammer591/exo-mimic">Hammer591/exo-mimic</a><a href="https://github.com/GWinfinity/cloud-robotics-sim"